course: dictionary
lesson: 11031
title: Who is "we"?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: "We" is a small word that stands for you and other people together. In «We are learning about pronouns», the speaker is one of the group. "Us" is the same idea in a different place in the sentence, as in «Come with us».
explain: "We" can also mean all people. «We need water to live» is true for everyone, not only the speaker. Sometimes "we" means the speaker's team or country: «We won!» can be said by someone who only cheered from the side.
explain: Look at the words around "we" to see who it means. «A newborn baby has more bones than an adult, because some bones join together as we grow» means everyone grows, not just the writer. In «Give us a hand», "us" means "me" in the UK and Australia, so it means help me.
explain: Writers in exams and reports may avoid "we". Instead they write «It is observed that», which sounds more formal. Casual talk can break the usual rules, as in «we was», but that is not standard English.
fact: "We" is a pronoun, so it takes the place of a name or a group of people.
fact: The forms are we, us, our, ours and ourselves.
fact: «Let's» is a short form of «let us», as in «Let's do it».
fact: "Our" shows that something belongs to us, as in «our class».
fact: «We don't want you here» can be unkind, because it leaves someone out.
exercise: «We need water to live.» Who does "we" mean here? | * All people, including everyone | A dog and a cat | Only the speaker | The teacher only
exercise: In «Give us a hand», what does "us" mean in the UK and Australia? | * Me, so it means help me | Everyone in the world | The speaker's team only | Two dogs
exercise: Which word is the possessive form of "we", as in «our class»? | us | they | you | * our
test: Pick the right word: «Come with ___ to the park.» | him | * us | they | she
test: Ana cheered from the side while her team played. Which word fits? «___ won the match!» | They | Him | * We | Us
exam: In a formal report, which sentence avoids "we"? | «We think the plants grew» | «We observe that the plants grew» | «Us saw the plants grew» | * «It is observed that the plants grew»
